### Principal Component Analysis (PCA) results of Psychological Scales

Regarding the characterization of the sample and the evaluation of differences in each scale, descriptive statistics and group comparisons revealed no statistically significant differences between adolescents and adults across any of the psychological scales after applying the FDR correction for multiple comparisons (@tbl-psico).

