### ROIs results

Initially, we performed between-group analyses within the three ROIs across all experimental conditions and contrasts to assess potential group differences. We found two notable findings, but they remain uncorrected. Specifically, in the bilateral NAcc, a marginal group difference was observed during the LR \> C contrast, where adults exhibited higher BOLD signal compared to adolescents (W = 342.0, puncorrected = .052, pFDR = .523), Wilcoxon r = .25, Mdn_Adults = 0.128, Mdn_Adolescents = 0.036). Additionally, a significant group difference was found in the bilateral insula for the LL \> C contrast, where adults demonstrated increased signal relative to adolescents (W = 327.0, p uncorrected = .031, p FDR = .310, Wilcoxon r = .27, Mdn_Adults = 0.041, Mdn_Adolescents = -0.037). However, neither of these effects survived False Discovery Rate (FDR) correction for multiple comparisons.

