Given that the behavioral results revealed a distinct bimodal distribution in total monetary payout, task performance profile was included as a nuisance covariate in the moderation models to effectively control for BOLD signal variance associated with individual performance profiles. Moderation analyses on the four conditions and six contrast-specific beta weights across all ROIs yielded three significant interactions after multiple comparison correction. Notably, all statistically significant effects were observed exclusively during the loss anticipation phase. Specifically, two effects were identified in the NAcc—for the overall Loss (HL + LL) \> C contrast and LL \> C contrast—while the remaining significant effect emerged in the thalamus during the LL condition. The specific statistical parameters for each of these analyses are detailed below.

```{r}
